  "scope": "Use finite-sum characterization for prefix uniqueness",
  "validation": "Paired target ArithmeticCellDecoding and direct client ArithmeticWholeField builds pass using refreshed current CellLocal and CellLabels objects. Rebuilt current CellTransfer against those objects produces exactly the direct object used. Eight object-pinned probes per phase report 69 common target declarations, 68 with identical type and axioms, one changed generated proof, two generated simp declarations removed and one proof added; 75 client declarations and sampled registrations match. Client objects differ.",
  "limitations": [
    "The target, direct client, and prior producer receipts do not establish a source-current transitive closure. Wider downstream clients were not rebuilt.",
    "The removed generated names and changed generated proof name have no references in tracked Lean/Python search. Declaration reports and sampled registrations do not prove equality of proof bodies or all persistent extensions.",
    "Compiled objects are omitted. Recorded build and probe paths refer to original temporary directories; full replay requires the external environment and object dependencies.",
    "Both target builds issue the same one warning and both client builds the same eleven warnings after phase path and line-number normalization.",
    "Original phase probe logs were omitted from the archive: recorded hashes match refreshed logs byte-for-byte, and original probe records are included."
  ],
  "archive": "inputs-and-logs.zip",
